      "role": "user",
      "content": "okay but isn't the other side actually more legally sound though? like if the president can't have total control over their internal communications, doesn't that basically destroy the separation of powers and make the executive branch subservient to whoever controls congress? feels like the \"erosion of checks\" argument is sometimes just a way to avoid looking at the actual legal necessity of presidential confidentiality.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
